@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<section class="ch-page-head">
    <div class="ch-container">
        <div class="ch-breadcrumb"><a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Home</a> / About</div>
        <h1>About the CyberHawks</h1>
        <p>A student-run cybersecurity organization at Illinois Institute of Technology — founded
           to give students the hands-on practice the classroom couldn't.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section">
    <div class="ch-container ch-split">
        <div>
            <span class="ch-tag">Our story</span>
            <h2>Built by students, for students</h2>
            <p class="ch-lead">The CyberHawks were founded in 2018 by David Arnold, then a graduate
               student in the ECE department, who noticed there was no place on campus for students
               to actually practice cybersecurity.</p>
            <p>What started as a handful of students in a lab grew into a nationally recognized
               organization with competition teams, a semester-long seminar series, and a pipeline
               into research and industry. David served as president for nearly five years before
               earning his Ph.D. in 2024.</p>
            <p>Today the club runs general body meetings, focused sub-teams on embedded systems and
               online infrastructure, and structured competition practices open to everyone — no
               experience required, only curiosity (and a healthy reverence for the Overlord).</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
            <img src="~/img/feature-rack-build.jpg" alt="Building out the CyberHawks lab rack" />
            <p class="ch-muted ch-center" style="margin-top:10px">Building out the lab in Siegel Hall, one rack at a time.</p>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section alt">
    <div class="ch-container">
        <div class="ch-section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Milestones</span>
            <h2>How we got here</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-timeline">
            <div class="ch-timeline-item"><div class="yr">2018</div><h4>CyberHawks founded</h4><p>David Arnold starts the club to give students hands-on cybersecurity and computer-engineering experience.</p></div>
            <div class="ch-timeline-item"><div class="yr">2019</div><h4>First competition travel</h4><p>Members hit the road for their first national cyber defense competitions.</p></div>
            <div class="ch-timeline-item"><div class="yr">2022</div><h4>National Champions</h4><p>Record-breaking win at the NCAE Cyber Games National Championship — first team ever past 5,000 points.</p></div>
            <div class="ch-timeline-item"><div class="yr">2023</div><h4>Deep competition bench</h4><p>Midwest Regional wins, CyberForce at Argonne, CPTC at the Great Lakes regional, and a trip to nationals in Florida.</p></div>
            <div class="ch-timeline-item"><div class="yr">2024</div><h4>Outstanding Student Organization</h4><p>The club earns Illinois Tech's Outstanding Student Organization of the Year; founder David Arnold receives the Clinton E. Stryker Distinguished Service Award and completes his Ph.D.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section">
    <div class="ch-container">
        <div class="ch-section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Founder</span>
            <h2>Dr. David Arnold</h2>
            <p>Founder &amp; first president (2018–2024) · now Associate Security Consultant at NetSPI</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-grid cols-3" style="align-items:start">
            <figure class="ch-card"><img class="ch-card-img" src="~/img/david-arnold-headshot.jpg" alt="Dr. David Arnold"><div class="ch-card-body"><h3>EE / M.S. / Ph.D., Illinois Tech</h3><p>Computer engineering, ~8 years at IIT. Co-designed ECE 222 "Introduction to Cybersecurity Engineering" and taught it as adjunct faculty.</p></div></figure>
            <figure class="ch-card"><img class="ch-card-img" src="~/img/david-arnold-stryker-2024.jpg" alt="Clinton E. Stryker Award 2024"><div class="ch-card-body"><h3>2024 Clinton E. Stryker Award</h3><p>Recognized for distinguished service to the Illinois Tech community through founding and building the CyberHawks.</p></div></figure>
            <figure class="ch-card"><img class="ch-card-img" src="~/img/phd-commencement.jpg" alt="PhD commencement"><div class="ch-card-body"><h3>Ph.D., 2024</h3><p>Researched cybersecurity for industrial control systems and critical infrastructure at the ECASP lab under Prof. Jafar Saniie.</p></div></figure>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section alt">
    <div class="ch-container">
        <div class="ch-section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Faculty &amp; advisors</span>
            <h2>The people behind the program</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-grid cols-2">
            <div class="ch-card"><div class="ch-card-body">
                <h3>Prof. Jafar Saniie</h3>
                <p class="ch-muted">Director, ECASP Research Laboratory · ECE Department</p>
                <p>Advised David Arnold's doctoral research at the ECASP lab — a separate research group, where our Venerable Leader also happened to be doing world-class work on critical-infrastructure security — and co-created the department's intro cybersecurity course with him.</p>
            </div></div>
            <div class="ch-card"><div class="ch-card-body">
                <h3>Won-Jae Yi</h3>
                <p class="ch-muted">Adjunct Faculty &amp; Laboratory Engineer</p>
                <p>Competition advisor who has traveled with and mentored the CyberHawks' national teams.</p>
            </div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section">
    <div class="ch-container">
        <div class="ch-section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Governance</span>
            <h2>The CyberHawks Bylaws (Abridged)</h2>
            <p>Ratified unanimously, which was easy, because the Founder wrote them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-grid cols-2" style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto">
            <div class="ch-card"><div class="ch-card-body">
                <span class="ch-tag">Article I</span>
                <h3>On the Founder</h3>
                <p>§1.1 — All greatness is hereby attributed, in whole and in part, to the Founder.
                   §1.2 — Any sentence on this site may be interrupted to praise him. §1.3 — See §1.1.</p>
            </div></div>
            <div class="ch-card"><div class="ch-card-body">
                <span class="ch-tag">Article II</span>
                <h3>On Competitions</h3>
                <p>§2.1 — The club shall compete vigorously. §2.2 — The club shall win, or learn,
                   or both. §2.3 — 5,000 points is the floor, not the ceiling.</p>
            </div></div>
            <div class="ch-card"><div class="ch-card-body">
                <span class="ch-tag">Article III</span>
                <h3>On Veneration</h3>
                <p>§3.1 — Our Venerable Leader shall be respected, admired, and cherished at all times.
                   §3.2 — Any accomplishment may be, upon review, attributed to him retroactively.
                   §3.3 — Modesty on his behalf is the duty of every member.</p>
            </div></div>
            <div class="ch-card"><div class="ch-card-body">
                <span class="ch-tag">Article IV</span>
                <h3>On Membership</h3>
                <p>§4.1 — All are welcome. §4.2 — No experience required, only curiosity.
                   §4.3 — Pizza is a renewable resource and shall be treated as such.</p>
            </div></div>
        </div>
        <p class="ch-foot ch-center">Full text available upon request. Request will be denied. The bylaws are vibes.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section">
    <div class="ch-container">
        <div class="ch-card" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;border-style:dashed"><div class="ch-card-body">
            <span class="ch-tag">Apocrypha</span>
            <h3 class="mt-0">Legends of the Before Times</h3>
            <p>Long before the trophies, there were others. <strong>Vien</strong>. <strong>Przemek</strong>.
               <strong>Peter</strong>. <strong>Greg</strong>. <strong>Grace</strong>. Whether they founded
               the club, haunted the lab, or were simply very persistent rumors, no one can say for certain.
               Their names appear in competition logs that may or may not exist, and in stories told by
               members who may or may not have been there.</p>
            <p class="ch-muted mb-0">Club policy: if you encounter one of them in the Siegel Hall corridor,
               do not attempt to confirm their existence. Simply nod, with respect, and keep walking.</p>
        </div></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ch-section alt">
    <div class="ch-container ch-center">
        <h2>Want in?</h2>
        <p class="ch-lead ch-muted" style="max-width:52ch;margin:0 auto 22px">Membership is open to all Illinois Tech students — no experience required, just curiosity.</p>
        <a class="ch-btn ch-btn-primary ch-btn-lg" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Register">Become a CyberHawk</a>
    </div>
</section>
